{"ts": "2026-08-17T11:59:42Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 31, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (31KB). Full output saved to: /home/dev/.claude/projects/-home-dev-projects-test-project/13b62a49-3056-4b0b-9995-aa9f55373289/tool-results/bq0zhjv9s.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\ndiff --git a/docs/design.md b/docs/design.md\nindex 7743b51..43476a4 100644\n--- a/docs/design.md\n+++ b/docs/design.md\n@@ -1,52 +1,221 @@\n-# Design: Keep my tasks when the server restarts\n-\n-Source: `docs/spec.md` (Taiga #5), as of the \"Decisions made here\" and\n-\"Acceptance criteria\" sections.\n-\n-## No design surface \u2014 this stage is a no-op\n-\n-Every acceptance criterion in `docs/spec.md` is satisfied entirely inside\n-`backend/app/store.py`'s persistence logic and `backend/app/main.py`'s\n-existing routes, which are explicitly unchanged (spec's \"Affected areas\":\n-*\"`backend/app/main.py` \u2014 no changes expected. Every route already goes\n-through `store`; persistence is invisible to the route layer.\"*).\n-\n-Checking against what this role covers:\n-\n-- **API surface** \u2014 every route's request/response shape is unchanged\n-  (spec non-goals: *\"No change to `backend/app/models.py` \u2014 the `Task`\n-  shape on the wire is unchanged\"*). Nothing for a client to render\n-  differently.\n-- **Frontend** \u2014 spec's \"Affected areas\" states plainly: *\"Not affected:\n-  `frontend/` (entire directory)\"*. There is no new screen, component,\n-  state, loading/error/empty case, or interaction to spec \u2014 the existing\n-  frontend already just calls `GET/POST/PATCH/DELETE /api/tasks*` and\n-  renders whatever comes back, and continues to do exactly that.\n-- **User-visible behavior change** \u2014 none, by design. The entire point of\n-  the feature (AC3, AC5, AC6) is that a restart is transparent: the app\n-  looks and behaves identically before and after this change, whether the\n-  data file is present, missing, or corrupt. There is no new state for a\n-  user to encounter \u2014 \"start empty on corrupt/missing data\" is not a new\n-  empty state UX, it's the *existing* empty-state UX (new task list, no\n-  tasks yet), reached via a different trigger.\n-\n-There is accordingly no wireframe, component tree change, styling\n-decision, or accessibility note to produce \u2014 introducing any would be\n...\n</persisted-output>", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_015sHu2B7jtoG5GuvvkEgUKZ", "session_id": "13b62a49-3056-4b0b-9995-aa9f55373289"}}
