{"ts": "2026-08-17T11:59:44Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 36, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "1\tdiff --git a/docs/design.md b/docs/design.md\n2\tindex 7743b51..43476a4 100644\n3\t--- a/docs/design.md\n4\t+++ b/docs/design.md\n5\t@@ -1,52 +1,221 @@\n6\t-# Design: Keep my tasks when the server restarts\n7\t-\n8\t-Source: `docs/spec.md` (Taiga #5), as of the \"Decisions made here\" and\n9\t-\"Acceptance criteria\" sections.\n10\t-\n11\t-## No design surface \u2014 this stage is a no-op\n12\t-\n13\t-Every acceptance criterion in `docs/spec.md` is satisfied entirely inside\n14\t-`backend/app/store.py`'s persistence logic and `backend/app/main.py`'s\n15\t-existing routes, which are explicitly unchanged (spec's \"Affected areas\":\n16\t-*\"`backend/app/main.py` \u2014 no changes expected. Every route already goes\n17\t-through `store`; persistence is invisible to the route layer.\"*).\n18\t-\n19\t-Checking against what this role covers:\n20\t-\n21\t-- **API surface** \u2014 every route's request/response shape is unchanged\n22\t-  (spec non-goals: *\"No change to `backend/app/models.py` \u2014 the `Task`\n23\t-  shape on the wire is unchanged\"*). Nothing for a client to render\n24\t-  differently.\n25\t-- **Frontend** \u2014 spec's \"Affected areas\" states plainly: *\"Not affected:\n26\t-  `frontend/` (entire directory)\"*. There is no new screen, component,\n27\t-  state, loading/error/empty case, or interaction to spec \u2014 the existing\n28\t-  frontend already just calls `GET/POST/PATCH/DELETE /api/tasks*` and\n29\t-  renders whatever comes back, and continues to do exactly that.\n30\t-- **User-visible behavior change** \u2014 none, by design. The entire point of\n31\t-  the feature (AC3, AC5, AC6) is that a restart is transparent: the app\n32\t-  looks and behaves identically before and after this change, whether the\n33\t-  data file is present, missing, or corrupt. There is no new state for a\n34\t-  user to encounter \u2014 \"start empty on corrupt/missing data\" is not a new\n35\t-  empty state UX, it's the *existing* empty-state UX (new task list, no\n36\t-  tasks yet), reached via a different trigger.\n37\t-\n38\t-There is accordingly no wireframe, component tree change, styling\n39\t-decision, or accessibility note to produce \u2014 introducing any would be\n40\t-inventing UI the story's own non-goals rule out (*\"No new HTTP endpoint...\n41\t-No frontend change\"*).\n42\t+# Design: Clear all completed tasks at once\n43\t+\n44\t+Taiga #9 \u00b7 for `docs/spec.md` (same ticket)\n45\t+\n46\t+## Conventions found (establishing the stack)\n47\t+\n48\t+- Plain function components, one per file, under `frontend/src/components/`.\n49\t+- Plain CSS in `frontend/src/App.css`, no framework, no CSS-in-JS, no design\n50\t+  token layer \u2014 colors and spacing are hand-picked literals reused by eye\n51\t+  (e.g. `#ccd2d6` for every border, `0.5rem 0.8rem` for every button's\n52\t+  padding).\n53\t+- Every button is a bare `<button>` using the global `button { \u2026 }` /\n54\t+  `button:disabled { opacity: 0.5; cursor: not-allowed; }` rules\n55\t+  (`frontend/src/App.css:16-23`). No button anywhere has its own color \u2014\n56\t+  `Edit`, `Done`, `Delete`, filter options, and `Add` all look the same\n57\t+  modulo the `.filter-option.active` state. **There is no \"destructive =\n58\t+  red\" convention in this app** \u2014 the existing per-task `Delete` button\n59\t+  (`TaskList.jsx:110-112`) is styled identically to `Edit`/`Done`.\n60\t+- No modal, `<dialog>`, or overlay pattern exists anywhere in this codebase.\n61\t+  Confirms the spec's non-goal: this control must not introduce one.\n62\t+- Handler-prop naming is consistently `on<Verb>` (`onComplete`, `onDelete`,\n63\t+  `onUpdate`, `onChange`) \u2014 new prop is `onClear`.\n64\t+- `TaskFilter` (`frontend/src/components/TaskFilter.jsx`) is the closest\n65\t+  sibling in shape: a small standalone control rendered directly in\n66\t+  `App.jsx` between the error banner and the list, not owned by any other\n67\t+  component.\n68\t+- No focus-ring override exists in `App.css` \u2014 browser default focus\n69\t+  styling is used app-wide. Not introducing one here either.\n70\t+- No in-flight/spinner state exists on any button in this app (`Add`,\n71\t+  `Complete`, `Delete`, `Save` all fire-and-await via `run()` with no busy\n72\t+  indicator). Not introducing one here either, for consistency.\n73\t+\n74\t+## New component\n75\t+\n76\t+`frontend/src/components/ClearCompleted.jsx` \u2014 one file, per convention.\n77\t+\n78\t+```jsx\n79\t+export default function ClearCompleted({ count, onClear }) {\n80\t+  return (\n81\t+    <button\n82\t+      type=\"button\"\n83\t+      className=\"clear-completed\"\n84\t+      disabled={count === 0}\n85\t+      onClick={onClear}\n86\t+    >\n87\t+      Clear completed ({count})\n88\t+    </button>\n89\t+  )\n90\t+}\n91\t+```\n92\t+\n93\t+Props: `count` (number), `onClear` (handler, no args \u2014 matches the\n94\t+zero-arg shape `onClear={() => run(() => api.clearCompleted())}` will take\n95\t+in `App.jsx`, same pattern as `AddTask`'s `onAdd`).\n96\t+\n97\t+No `aria-label` needed: unlike `Edit`/`Delete`/`Complete` in `TaskList`,\n98\t+which need one because their visible text (\"Delete\") doesn't say *which*\n99\t+task, this button's own text already states the full action and count \u2014\n100\t+that text **is** its accessible name.\n101\t+\n102\t+## Placement and layout\n103\t+\n104\t+Render as a sibling of `TaskFilter`, not nested inside it \u2014 this is a\n105\t+deliberate visual signal for **AC4** (the action is store-wide, not\n106\t+filter-scoped): if it lived inside or under the filter control it would\n107\t+visually imply \"clear completed *within this filter view*,\" which is\n108\t+false. Introduce one new wrapper row so both sit on one line, right-aligned\n109\t+against the filter:\n110\t+\n111\t+`frontend/src/App.jsx` \u2014 replace the standalone `<TaskFilter .../>` line\n112\t+with:\n113\t+\n114\t+```jsx\n115\t+<div className=\"list-toolbar\">\n116\t+  <TaskFilter value={filter} onChange={setFilter} />\n117\t+  <ClearCompleted count={completedCount} onClear={() => run(() => api.clearCompleted())} />\n118\t+</div>\n119\t+```\n120\t+\n121\t+where `completedCount = tasks.filter((t) => t.done).length`, computed from\n122\t+the full `tasks` array (already specified in `docs/spec.md`'s Affected\n123\t+areas) \u2014 same value in both the \"before action\" display (AC2) and the\n124\t+\"store-wide, not view-scoped\" guarantee (AC4), because it never reads\n125\t+`visibleTasks`.\n126\t+\n127\t+`frontend/src/App.css` \u2014 new rule:\n128\t+\n129\t+```css\n130\t+.list-toolbar {\n131\t+  display: flex;\n132\t+  justify-content: space-between;\n133\t+  align-items: center;\n134\t+  flex-wrap: wrap;\n135\t+  gap: 0.6rem;\n136\t+  margin-bottom: 1.2rem;\n137\t+}\n138\t+.list-toolbar .task-filter { margin-bottom: 0; }\n139\t+```\n140\t+\n141\t+`.task-filter` already carries `margin-bottom: 1.2rem` (`App.css:38`) for\n142\t+its old standalone placement; the override above prevents doubled spacing\n143\t+now that the parent `.list-toolbar` owns that margin. `ClearCompleted`'s\n144\t+button needs no new rule of its own \u2014 it inherits the global `button` /\n145\t+`button:disabled` styling, which is the point (no new visual language for\n146\t+\"destructive,\" per the convention check above).\n147\t+\n148\t+`flex-wrap: wrap` is the adaptive behavior for the narrow (`max-width:\n149\t+34rem`, effectively mobile-width) container: if both controls don't fit\n150\t+one line, `ClearCompleted` drops to its own line below `TaskFilter` rather\n151\t+than truncating or overlapping. No breakpoint needed \u2014 the container is\n152\t+already narrow at every viewport.\n153\t+\n154\t+## States\n155\t+\n156\t+**Empty (0 completed) \u2014 AC1**\n157\t+```\n158\t+[ All | Open | Done ]         [ Clear completed (0) ]   \u2190 disabled, dimmed\n159\t+```\n160\t+`disabled` is set directly from `count === 0`; no click handler runs, so\n161\t+\"clicking it (if somehow triggered) makes no API call\" is structurally\n162\t+true \u2014 a disabled `<button>` fires no `onClick` in the DOM, not just\n163\t+visually inert.\n164\t+\n165\t+**Loading (initial fetch, before first `refresh()` resolves)**\n166\t+\n167\t+`TaskFilter` already renders unconditionally above the\n168\t+`loading ? <p className=\"loading\">\u2026</p> : <TaskList .../>` branch in\n169\t+`App.jsx` (lines 53-65) \u2014 it doesn't wait for data. `ClearCompleted` joins\n170\t+it in the same unconditional `.list-toolbar` row, for the same reason:\n171\t+`tasks` starts as `[]`, so `completedCount` is `0` and the button renders\n172\t+disabled. This is visually identical to the empty state above and that's\n173\t+correct \u2014 before any data has loaded, \"0 completed\" is truthful, not a\n174\t+placeholder guess. No separate loading treatment for this control.\n175\t+\n176\t+**Populated \u2014 AC2**\n177\t+```\n178\t+[ All | Open | Done ]         [ Clear completed (3) ]   \u2190 enabled\n179\t+```\n180\t+One completed: `Clear completed (1)`. Many completed (e.g. 47): the label\n181\t+is just a number, no truncation/\"99+\" logic needed \u2014 nothing in the spec\n182\t+or this app's scale implies large counts.\n183\t+\n184\t+**All tasks completed, then cleared**\n185\t+\n186\t+List becomes empty after the action. No new empty-state copy: the\n187\t+existing `EMPTY_COPY` in `TaskList.jsx:3-7` already handles it per the\n188\t+active filter (`\"Nothing to do yet.\"` / `\"Nothing open right now.\"` /\n189\t+`\"Nothing done yet.\"`) \u2014 this path was already reachable via one-at-a-time\n190\t+Delete, so it's already correct.\n191\t+\n192\t+**Error (API call fails mid-clear)**\n193\t+\n194\t+No new UI. `onClear` is wired through the existing `run()` helper\n195\t+(`App.jsx:37-46`), which on rejection calls `setError(e.message)` and\n196\t+renders the existing `<p className=\"error\" role=\"alert\">` banner\n197\t+(`App.jsx:52`) \u2014 identical path to a failed `Delete`. The button itself\n198\t+returns to its normal enabled state (no local pending flag is introduced,\n199\t+so there's nothing to reset). `count` is unchanged because `refresh()`\n200\t+never ran, so the pre-click count is still shown, which is the truthful\n201\t+count.\n202\t+\n203\t+**Interactive**\n204\t+\n205\t+- *Default / hover*: base `button` styling, no new rule \u2014 matches\n206\t+  `Edit`/`Done`/`Delete`.\n207\t+- *Focus*: browser default outline, unmodified (no `:focus` rule exists\n208\t+  anywhere in `App.css` to be consistent with).\n209\t+- *Disabled*: `button:disabled { opacity: 0.5; cursor: not-allowed; }`\n210\t+  (`App.css:23`), the exact rule already applied to `Add` when its input is\n211\t+  empty. This reuses an existing token/rule verbatim rather than\n212\t+  introducing a new color pairing, so no fresh contrast computation\n213\t+  applies \u2014 the enabled-state pairing it inherits from is checked below.\n214\t+\n215\t+## Accessibility\n216\t+\n217\t+- **Target size**: same `padding: 0.5rem 0.8rem` as every other button in\n218\t+  the app (~36px effective height at the default 16px body font) \u2014 no new\n219\t+  sizing decision, reusing the established value.\n220\t+- **Focus order**: `ClearCompleted` sits immediately after `TaskFilter`'s\n221\t+  three buttons in DOM order (sibling in `.list-toolbar`, declared second),\n222\t+  so tab order is All \u2192 Open \u2192 Done \u2192 Clear completed \u2192 (task rows) \u2014\n223\t+  matches visual left-to-right reading order.\n224\t+- **Contrast** (enabled state, the pairing every other button in this app\n225\t+  already uses \u2014 verifying it here since this is the first time it's being\n226\t+  stated numerically): text `#16191c` on background `#fff`, both existing\n227\t+  literals from `App.css`. Relative luminance: `#16191c` \u2248 0.0097, `#fff` =\n228\t+  1.0. Contrast ratio = (1.0 + 0.05) / (0.0097 + 0.05) \u2248 **17.5:1** \u2014 passes\n229\t+  the 4.5:1 text threshold with large margin. Border `#ccd2d6` on `#fff`\n230\t+  background (non-text, 3:1 threshold): luminance of `#ccd2d6` \u2248 0.716,\n231\t+  ratio = (1.0 + 0.05) / (0.716 + 0.05) \u2248 **1.37:1** \u2014 this fails 3:1, but\n232\t+  it is the exact same border already used on every other button, input,\n233\t+  and the filter group in this app; not a new pairing introduced by this\n234\t+  feature, so there's nothing to adjust here without relitigating the\n235\t+  whole app's existing button chrome, which is out of scope for this\n236\t+  ticket.\n237\t+- **Screen reader**: accessible name is the full button text, \"Clear\n238\t+  completed (N)\" \u2014 states the action and the count together, so no\n239\t+  separate `aria-live` announcement is needed for \"how many it will\n240\t+  remove\" (AC2's requirement is satisfied by the visible/accessible label\n241\t+  itself, not a dynamic announcement).\n242\t \n243\t ## Acceptance criteria traceability\n244\t \n245\t-| AC | Why no design element applies |\n246\t-|----|-------------------------------|\n247\t-| 1\u20132 | Write-on-mutation happens inside `TaskStore` methods, called from existing routes with no response shape change |\n248\t-| 3\u20134 | Load-on-construct happens before the app serves any request; `GET /api/tasks` response shape is unchanged, so the existing frontend list rendering already handles it with no modification |\n249\t-| 5\u20136 | \"Start empty\" is the app's current first-run/no-tasks appearance already \u2014 no new empty state to design |\n250\t-| 7 | Directory creation is filesystem-internal, no observable surface |\n251\t-| 8 | Test hermeticity is a backend test-infra concern, not a design concern |\n252\t+| AC | Design element |\n253\t+|----|-----------------|\n254\t+| 1 (0 completed \u2192 disabled, count 0, inert) | `disabled={count === 0}` in `ClearCompleted.jsx`; Empty state above |\n255\t+| 2 (count shown before action runs) | Label reads `count` from render-time `completedCount`, which only changes after `refresh()` completes post-`onClear` |\n256\t+| 3 (no `done:true` after) | Backend-only, no visual dimension |\n257\t+| 4 (store-wide, not filter-scoped) | `ClearCompleted` is a sibling of `TaskFilter`, not nested in/gated by it; `completedCount` sourced from full `tasks`, not `visibleTasks` \u2014 see Placement section |\n258\t+| 5 (persists across restart) | Backend-only, no visual dimension |\n259\t+| 6 (empty store \u2192 200/count 0) | Backend-only; front-end behavior is identical to the Empty state (button already disabled, no call ever fires) |\n260\t \n261\t-## Handoff\n262\t+## What this does not touch\n263\t \n264\t-Straight to **developer** \u2014 implement `docs/spec.md` as written, no\n265\t-`docs/design.md` decisions to consume beyond this note confirming there\n266\t-are none.\n267\t+- No confirmation dialog \u2014 non-goal, and no precedent exists in this app to\n268\t+  build one from.\n269\t+- No new color, icon, or button variant for \"destructive\" actions \u2014\n270\t+  `Delete`, and now `Clear completed`, both use the same plain button as\n271\t+  every non-destructive action.\n272\t+- `TaskList`'s empty-state copy is unchanged; the existing per-filter\n273\t+  strings already cover the post-clear empty case.\n274\tdiff --git a/docs/spec.md b/docs/spec.md\n275\tindex 98822b1..50292cc 100644\n276\t--- a/docs/spec.md\n277\t+++ b/docs/spec.md\n278\t@@ -1,156 +1,134 @@\n279\t-# Spec: Keep my tasks when the server restarts\n280\t+# Spec: Clear all completed tasks at once\n281\t \n282\t-Taiga #5\n283\t+Taiga #9\n284\t+\n285\t+## Workspace check\n286\t+\n287\t+`git status` is clean, `git log` shows the branch tip (`9c6eea4`) is the\n288\t+already-merged \"Keep tasks when the server restarts\" (Taiga #5) work. No\n289\t+foreign in-progress work in the tree. `docs/spec.md` and `docs/design.md`\n290\t+were leftover from that finished Taiga #5 cycle, already merged, so there's\n291\t+nothing to lose. This spec overwrites `spec.md`; `design.md` is left as-is\n292\t+for the ux-designer stage to overwrite in turn.\n293\t \n294\t ## Triage\n295\t \n296\t-**Feature** \u2014 net-new capability, but purely additive at the persistence\n297\t-layer. Touches only `backend/app/store.py`, backend test setup, and\n298\t-`.gitignore`. No route changes, no request/response shape changes, no\n299\t-frontend changes \u2014 every existing endpoint already goes through\n300\t-`TaskStore`, so persistence is transparent underneath it. Single\n301\t-architectural layer (data/store), so this stays one spec, not split into a\n302\t-sequence.\n303\t+**Feature** \u2014 net-new capability. Touches three layers (store, route,\n304\t+frontend), but each layer is a thin, additive slice of an established\n305\t+pattern already used by every other mutation (`complete_task`,\n306\t+`delete_task`, etc.) \u2014 there's no new architectural concept to introduce.\n307\t+Keeping this as one spec rather than splitting: the \"split across layers\"\n308\t+rule exists to stop one cycle from carrying disproportionate weight, and\n309\t+here the backend half is ~15 lines across two files and the frontend half is\n310\t+one new ~20-line component plus two call sites. Splitting would produce two\n311\t+reviews of trivial, mutually-meaningless partial features.\n312\t \n313\t ## Goal\n314\t \n315\t-A task created (or completed, retitled, reprioritized, deleted) survives a\n316\t-server restart \u2014 nothing is lost just because the process stopped.\n317\t+Let me remove every completed task in one action, instead of deleting them\n318\t+one at a time.\n319\t \n320\t ## Acceptance criteria\n321\t \n322\t-1. Given the server is running, when a task is created via\n323\t-   `POST /api/tasks`, then the full task list is written to the data file\n324\t-   before the response is returned, so reading the file afterward reflects\n325\t-   the new task.\n326\t-2. Given step 1, and any of `POST /api/tasks/{id}/done`,\n327\t-   `PATCH /api/tasks/{id}`, `PATCH /api/tasks/{id}/priority`, or\n328\t-   `DELETE /api/tasks/{id}` \u2014 each of these also writes the full task list\n329\t-   to disk synchronously as part of the request, not deferred or batched.\n330\t-   A restart immediately after any one of these does not lose that change.\n331\t-3. Given a data file on disk containing previously-saved tasks, when the\n332\t-   server starts, then those tasks are loaded into the store with `id`,\n333\t-   `title`, `done`, and `priority` all intact, and `GET /api/tasks` returns\n334\t-   them immediately, with no client action required.\n335\t-4. Given tasks were loaded from disk with the highest id being `N`, when a\n336\t-   new task is created, then its id is `N + 1` \u2014 the id counter picks up\n337\t-   from the persisted data, never restarting at 1 and never colliding with\n338\t-   a loaded id.\n339\t-5. Given the data file does not exist (first run, or it was deleted), when\n340\t-   the server starts, then the store starts empty, no error is raised, and\n341\t-   the server serves requests normally \u2014 identical to today's behaviour\n342\t-   before this feature existed.\n343\t-6. Given the data file exists but is not valid JSON, or is valid JSON that\n344\t-   doesn't match the expected shape (e.g. a JSON object instead of an\n345\t-   array, an empty file, or an array of the wrong item shape), when the\n346\t-   server starts, then the store starts empty, no exception propagates out\n347\t-   of startup, and the server serves requests normally.\n348\t-7. Given the configured data directory doesn't exist yet, when the first\n349\t-   write happens, then the directory is created automatically rather than\n350\t-   raising `FileNotFoundError`.\n351\t-8. Backend tests remain hermetic: they never read or write the real data\n352\t-   file used by a locally-running server, and each test still starts from\n353\t-   an empty store, matching today's `_clean_store` autouse fixture\n354\t-   behaviour.\n355\t+1. **Given** zero completed tasks exist, **when** I look at the clear-completed\n356\t+   control, **then** it is disabled and shows a count of 0; clicking it (if\n357\t+   somehow triggered) makes no API call and removes nothing.\n358\t+2. **Given** N completed tasks and M open tasks (N > 0), **when** I trigger\n359\t+   clear-completed, **then** exactly N tasks are removed, all M open tasks\n360\t+   are unchanged (same id, title, priority, done=false), and the control's\n361\t+   count reflects N before the action runs.\n362\t+3. **Given** clear-completed has just run, **when** I `GET /api/tasks`,\n363\t+   **then** no task in the response has `done: true`.\n364\t+4. **Given** the current list filter is \"open\" or \"done\" (not \"all\"),\n365\t+   **when** I trigger clear-completed, **then** it still removes every\n366\t+   completed task store-wide \u2014 the action is not scoped to what's currently\n367\t+   visible under the filter.\n368\t+5. **Given** clear-completed has just run, **when** the server restarts\n369\t+   (store reloads from `TASKS_DATA_FILE`), **then** the removed tasks do not\n370\t+   reappear \u2014 the on-disk snapshot reflects the removal, same guarantee\n371\t+   every other mutation already gives (Taiga #5).\n372\t+6. **Given** the task list is entirely empty (no tasks at all, not just no\n373\t+   completed ones), **when** `DELETE /api/tasks/completed` is called\n374\t+   directly, **then** it returns `200` with a count of `0`, not an error.\n375\t \n376\t ## Non-goals\n377\t \n378\t-- No new HTTP endpoint for export/import/backup of the data file \u2014 this is\n379\t-  an internal implementation detail, not a new API surface.\n380\t-- No database. A JSON file is still not a database; introducing one is\n381\t-  explicitly called out in `backend/app/store.py`'s own docstring as \"a\n382\t-  decision, not an implementation detail,\" and this spec doesn't make that\n383\t-  decision.\n384\t-- No multi-process or multi-worker file locking. This app runs as a single\n385\t-  `uvicorn` process today (`--reload` included); concurrent writers to the\n386\t-  same file are not a scenario this app creates.\n387\t-- No partial recovery of a corrupt file (e.g. salvaging the valid entries\n388\t-  out of a partially-truncated JSON array). \"Corrupt \u2192 start empty\" is the\n389\t-  entire recovery story per the request; anything more is out of scope.\n390\t-- No versioning/backup of previous file contents (no `.bak` rotation).\n391\t-- No frontend change \u2014 the UI already just calls the existing endpoints and\n392\t-  reflects whatever the backend returns.\n393\t-- No change to `backend/app/models.py` \u2014 the `Task` shape on the wire is\n394\t-  unchanged; only its at-rest serialization is new.\n395\t+- No undo. This mirrors the existing per-task Delete button, which is also\n396\t+  irreversible.\n397\t+- No confirmation modal / `window.confirm` dialog. Nothing else in this app\n398\t+  interrupts a destructive action with a popup (per-task Delete doesn't\n399\t+  either); \"tells me how many it will remove\" is satisfied by the count\n400\t+  being visible on the control before it's clicked, not by a popup.\n401\t+- No selective clearing (by priority, by age, by title match) \u2014 \"every\n402\t+  completed task,\" full stop.\n403\t+- No keyboard shortcut.\n404\t+- No change to how individual tasks are completed or deleted.\n405\t \n406\t ## Affected areas\n407\t \n408\t-Backend:\n409\t-- `backend/app/store.py` \u2014 `TaskStore.__init__` gains a data-file path\n410\t-  (resolved from an environment variable with a fixed default, see\n411\t-  decision below) and, on construction, attempts to load existing tasks\n412\t-  from that path. Every mutating method \u2014 `add` (line ~19), `set_done`\n413\t-  (~30), `set_priority` (~35), `update_title` (~40), `delete` (~45), and\n414\t-  `reset` (~49, used by tests) \u2014 writes the full current task list to disk\n415\t-  after mutating in-memory state. `_next_id` initializes to\n416\t-  `max(loaded task ids, default=0) + 1` instead of always `1`.\n417\t-- `backend/app/main.py` \u2014 no changes expected. Every route already goes\n418\t-  through `store`; persistence is invisible to the route layer.\n419\t-- `backend/data/` (new directory, not currently present) \u2014 default home\n420\t-  for `tasks.json`. Created on first write if missing (AC7).\n421\t-- `backend/tests/conftest.py` \u2014 set the data-file env var to a `pytest`\n422\t-  tmp path **before** `from app.main import app` runs (line 9), since that\n423\t-  import is what constructs the module-level `store` singleton and its\n424\t-  path is fixed at construction time. Without this, tests would load from\n425\t-  and write to the real data file.\n426\t-- `backend/tests/test_persistence.py` (new file, since this concern isn't\n427\t-  a single route \u2014 no natural `test_<route>.py` fit) \u2014 covers: state\n428\t-  surviving across two `TaskStore` instances pointed at the same tmp path\n429\t-  (simulating a restart), missing file starts empty, corrupt/malformed\n430\t-  file starts empty, id counter continuing correctly after reload, and\n431\t-  directory auto-creation.\n432\t-- `.gitignore` \u2014 add `backend/data/` so persisted task data is never\n433\t-  committed.\n434\t-\n435\t-Not affected: `frontend/` (entire directory), `backend/app/models.py`.\n436\t-\n437\t-## Decisions made here (not left open)\n438\t-\n439\t-1. **Data file location:** `backend/data/tasks.json`, resolved relative to\n440\t-   `store.py`'s own location (`Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent /\n441\t-   \"data\" / \"tasks.json\"`) rather than the process's current working\n442\t-   directory \u2014 so it resolves the same way whether uvicorn is started from\n443\t-   `backend/` (per this project's README) or elsewhere.\n444\t-2. **Override mechanism:** an environment variable (e.g. `TASKS_DATA_FILE`)\n445\t-   overrides the default path when set. This is the hook `conftest.py`\n446\t-   uses to redirect tests to an isolated tmp path \u2014 without it, tests and\n447\t-   the real running server would contend for the same file.\n448\t-3. **Write strategy:** synchronous, full-snapshot write on every mutation\n449\t-   (serialize the whole task list to JSON and write it), matching this\n450\t-   store's already-small scale (in-memory dict, no batching elsewhere).\n451\t-   Chosen over a write-ahead/append log as the simplest thing that\n452\t-   satisfies the acceptance criteria \u2014 this store has never optimized for\n453\t-   write volume and shouldn't start here.\n454\t-4. **Corrupt-file handling:** any exception raised while reading or\n455\t-   parsing the file at startup (`FileNotFoundError`, `json.JSONDecodeError`,\n456\t-   or a shape mismatch such as the parsed value not being a list of\n457\t-   objects with the expected keys) is caught at load time and treated\n458\t-   identically to \"no file\" \u2014 start empty. This is one code path, not two,\n459\t-   since the request draws no distinction between \"missing\" and \"corrupt.\"\n460\t+- `backend/app/store.py` \u2014 add `TaskStore.clear_completed() -> int`,\n461\t+  following the exact shape of `delete()`/`set_done()`: mutate `self._tasks`,\n462\t+  call `self._save()` once if anything changed, return the number removed.\n463\t+- `backend/app/models.py` \u2014 add a response model (no bare dicts, per\n464\t+  convention), e.g. `ClearResult(BaseModel)` with a single `count: int`\n465\t+  field.\n466\t+- `backend/app/main.py` \u2014 add `DELETE /api/tasks/completed`, response_model\n467\t+  `ClearResult`, calling `store.clear_completed()`.\n468\t+  **Ordering hazard, confirmed while reading this file**: the existing\n469\t+  `@app.delete(\"/api/tasks/{task_id}\")` at line 56 has no `:int` converter\n470\t+  in the path string, so Starlette matches `/api/tasks/completed` against it\n471\t+  as a plain string first (converter mismatch happens at\n472\t+  FastAPI's pydantic-validation stage, not at route-matching), producing a\n473\t+  `422` for `task_id=\"completed\"` instead of ever reaching a route\n474\t+  registered later. The new route **must** be declared above line 56, not\n475\t+  below it.\n476\t+- `backend/tests/test_tasks.py` \u2014 new tests alongside the existing\n477\t+  `test_<behavior>` style (see e.g. lines 34\u201341 for the delete-single\n478\t+  pattern).\n479\t+- `frontend/src/api.js` \u2014 add `clearCompleted = () => request('/api/tasks/completed', { method: 'DELETE' })`, same one-liner shape as the existing exports.\n480\t+- `frontend/src/components/` \u2014 one new component file for the control\n481\t+  (one component per file, per project convention). Exact placement/copy is\n482\t+  the ux-designer's call; functionally it needs the completed count and an\n483\t+  onClear handler.\n484\t+- `frontend/src/App.jsx` \u2014 compute `completedCount = tasks.filter(t =>\n485\t+  t.done).length` (note: from the full `tasks` list, not `visibleTasks` \u2014\n486\t+  ties to AC4, the control's count must not be filter-scoped), render the\n487\t+  new control, wire its handler through the existing `run()` helper\n488\t+  (line 37) so errors surface through the existing `error` banner\n489\t+  (line 52) the same way every other action already does.\n490\t+- `frontend/src/App.css` \u2014 styling for the new control, matching existing\n491\t+  button conventions (lines 16\u201323).\n492\t \n493\t ## Edge cases\n494\t \n495\t-- Missing file on startup \u2192 start empty (AC5).\n496\t-- Corrupt/unparseable JSON on startup \u2192 start empty (AC6).\n497\t-- Valid JSON but wrong top-level shape (object instead of array) \u2192 treated\n498\t-  as corrupt, start empty.\n499\t-- Valid JSON array but entries missing required fields or with the wrong\n500\t-  types \u2192 treated as corrupt, start empty (no per-entry salvage, per\n501\t-  non-goals).\n502\t-- Empty file (0 bytes) \u2192 invalid JSON, treated as corrupt, start empty.\n503\t-- `backend/data/` directory doesn't exist yet \u2192 created automatically on\n504\t-  first write (AC7), not just documented as a manual setup step.\n505\t-- Tasks loaded with non-contiguous ids (e.g. `1, 3, 7` after prior\n506\t-  deletes) \u2192 next created task gets `8`, not `4` or `1` (AC4).\n507\t-- Rapid restart immediately after a mutation \u2192 the file already reflects\n508\t-  it, since writes are synchronous per-request, not batched/delayed.\n509\t-- Running the test suite must never read or write\n510\t-  `backend/data/tasks.json` on a developer's machine, even if that file\n511\t-  already exists from a real run (AC8).\n512\t+- Zero completed tasks: control is inert (AC1). No API call fires.\n513\t+- All tasks are completed: list becomes empty afterward, same empty-state\n514\t+  copy path already used elsewhere (`TaskList`'s `EMPTY_COPY`).\n515\t+- Mixed completed/open: only completed removed, open tasks' ids/order\n516\t+  untouched (AC2).\n517\t+- Action triggered while a filter other than \"all\" is active: still\n518\t+  store-wide (AC4).\n519\t+- Backend restart after clearing: removal persists (AC5).\n520\t+- Direct API call against an already-empty store: `200`/count `0`, not a\n521\t+  404 or error (AC6) \u2014 there's no per-item id here to 404 against, unlike\n522\t+  the single-delete route.\n523\t+- Network/API failure mid-clear: surfaces through the existing `error` state\n524\t+  in `App.jsx`, same as every other mutation \u2014 no new error-handling path\n525\t+  needed.\n526\t \n527\t ## Open questions\n528\t \n529\t-None \u2014 the choices that would normally be open (file location, override\n530\t-mechanism, write strategy, corrupt-file handling) are resolved above under\n531\t-\"Decisions made here,\" since none of them changes this spec's scope and a\n532\t-reasonable default exists for each.\n533\t+- **How the count is communicated** (\"tells me how many it will remove\"):\n534\t+  proceeding under the assumption that an inline, always-visible count on\n535\t+  the control (e.g. a label showing the number) satisfies this, rather than\n536\t+  a confirmation dialog \u2014 justified above under Non-goals, since no other\n537\t+  destructive action in this app uses a dialog. If the actual product intent\n538\t+  was a pre-delete confirmation step, that's a different, larger UI pattern\n539\t+  this app doesn't have anywhere yet and would need sign-off before the\n540\t+  ux-designer builds it \u2014 override here if that reading is wrong.\n541\t+- **Response shape for the bulk-clear endpoint**: proceeding under a new\n542\t+  `ClearResult{count: int}` model (200 OK) rather than reusing `Task`'s\n543\t+  204-no-content convention from single delete, because this route has no\n544\t+  single task id to report \u2014 flagging in case a different contract (e.g.\n545\t+  returning the list of removed task ids) is wanted for some downstream\n546\t+  consumer; nothing in this codebase currently needs that.\n547\tdiff --git a/frontend/src/App.css b/frontend/src/App.css\n548\tindex bfa8d52..0975dbb 100644\n549\t--- a/frontend/src/App.css\n550\t+++ b/frontend/src/App.css\n551\t@@ -30,6 +30,16 @@ button:disabled { opacity: 0.5; cursor: not-allowed; }\n552\t .task-title { flex: 1; }\n553\t .task.done .task-title { text-decoration: line-through; opacity: 0.55; }\n554\t \n555\t+.list-toolbar {\n556\t+  display: flex;\n557\t+  justify-content: space-between;\n558\t+  align-items: center;\n559\t+  flex-wrap: wrap;\n560\t+  gap: 0.6rem;\n561\t+  margin-bottom: 1.2rem;\n562\t+}\n563\t+.list-toolbar .task-filter { margin-bottom: 0; }\n564\t+\n565\t .task-filter {\n566\t   display: inline-flex;\n567\t   border: 1px solid #ccd2d6;\n568\tdiff --git a/frontend/src/App.jsx b/frontend/src/App.jsx\n569\tindex dee07bd..6550866 100644\n570\t--- a/frontend/src/App.jsx\n571\t+++ b/frontend/src/App.jsx\n572\t@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@\n573\t 